(RESERVE BANK OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(DEPARTMENT OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(RBI/2024-25/125 DoS.CO.CSITE.REC.19/31.01.015/2024-25) Tj
T*
(September 18, 2024) Tj
T*
(Master Direction on Information Technology Governance and Cyber Resilience) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Chief Information Security Officer \(CISO\): Every Regulated Entity shall appoint a qualified, full-time CISO who shall be) Tj
T*
(an officer in the rank of General Manager or equivalent. The CISO shall report directly to the Executive Director or to the Board) Tj
T*
(Information Technology Committee, and shall have independent authority over cybersecurity posture and incident response.) Tj
T*
(2. Cyber Incident Reporting Timelines: All cybersecurity incidents of severity High or Critical \(including ransomware infections,) Tj
T*
(unauthorized intrusions, credential leaks, and core system outages\) must be reported to the Reserve Bank's Cyber Security Operation) Tj
T*
(Centre \(CSOC\) within six hours of detection. A detailed Root Cause Analysis \(RCA\) report must be submitted within 21 calendar days.) Tj
T*
(3. Security Operations Centre \(SOC\): Regulated Entities must establish and maintain an in-house or managed SOC operational on a) Tj
T*
(continuous 24x7x365 basis. The SOC must ingest logs from all core applications, firewalls, and Active Directory servers, retaining) Tj
T*
(tamper-evident audit logs for a minimum duration of one year online and three years in cold archive.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 1009 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Multi-Factor Authentication \(MFA\): Multi-factor authentication is mandatory for all administrative access, database logins,) Tj
T*
(VPN connections, and remote access to critical infrastructure. SMS-only OTP is not considered adequate for privileged administrative) Tj
T*
(sessions; hardware security keys or authenticator app tokens must be enforced.) Tj
T*
(5. Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing \(VAPT\): Comprehensive VAPT of all Internet-facing applications and core banking) Tj
T*
(systems must be conducted at least once every six months by CERT-In empanelled auditors. Critical vulnerabilities identified must be) Tj
T*
(remediated within 15 calendar days of receipt of the audit report.) Tj
T*
(6. Board Information Technology Committee: The Board of Directors of every bank shall constitute an IT Committee comprising at least) Tj
T*
(one independent director with demonstrated expertise in computer science or enterprise IT infrastructure.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 861 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. Cyber Crisis Management Plan \(CCMP\): Every bank shall formulate a comprehensive CCMP approved by the Board. Tabletop cyber) Tj
T*
(crisis simulation exercises and red-teaming drills must be conducted at least once annually involving senior executive management.) Tj
T*
(8. Patch Management Timelines: High and critical security patches released by original equipment manufacturers \(OEMs\) must be tested) Tj
T*
(and deployed within seven calendar days of release. Zero-day vulnerability mitigations must be activated within 24 hours.) Tj
T*
(9. Data Loss Prevention \(DLP\): Endpoint and network DLP solutions must be implemented to prevent unauthorized exfiltration of sensitive) Tj
T*
(customer data, personal identifiers, and financial records through USB storage, personal email, or cloud file-sharing services.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 898 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(10. Critical Information Infrastructure \(CII\): Systems processing high-value payment transactions, RTGS/NEFT interfaces, and) Tj
T*
(core banking transaction engines shall be declared as Critical Information Infrastructure under Section 70 of the IT Act, 2000.) Tj
T*
(11. Secure Software Development Life Cycle \(SSDLC\): All in-house applications and third-party software customizations must adhere to) Tj
T*
(SSDLC guidelines, including static application security testing \(SAST\) and dynamic analysis \(DAST\) prior to production deployment.) Tj
T*
(12. Third-Party Vendor Security: Contracts with technology vendors must include clauses granting the Reserve Bank the right to audit) Tj
T*
(vendor infrastructure supporting the bank's outsourced operations.) Tj
T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj
T*
(\(P. V. Narayanan\)) Tj
T*
(Chief General Manager-in-Charge) Tj
T*
ET
